{
  "description": "The published server is `https://{topicId}.pubsub.eu01.onstackit.cloud`: a topic is its own host, and no operation can name it. The official Go client builds that host from the topic id and region itself (`pkg/pubsub/publisher.go`, `subscriber.go`, read 2026-11-01). Add the topic and region to each input as labels, under the management API's names. `src/protocol.ts` fills them into the host; the routes don't mention them, so they stay out of the path and the body.",
  "patches": [
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/shapes/com.stackit.pubsub_data#PublishMessagesRequest/members/topicId",
      "value": {
        "target": "smithy.api#String",
        "traits": {
          "smithy.api#httpLabel": {},
          "smithy.api#required": {},
          "smithy.api#documentation": "The topic UUID. Part of the host, not the path."
        }
      }
    },
    {
